A song should be removed exactly when it is in the initial song library but in neither the liked-song set nor the downloaded-song set; the candidate IDs must be reviewed before mutation.

```python
initial_song_library_ids = {record['song_id'] for record in song_library_records}
liked_song_ids = {record['song_id'] for record in liked_song_records}
downloaded_song_ids = {record['song_id'] for record in downloaded_song_records}
song_keep_ids = initial_song_library_ids & (liked_song_ids | downloaded_song_ids)
song_removal_ids = sorted(initial_song_library_ids - song_keep_ids)
print({'song_removal_count': len(song_removal_ids), 'song_removal_ids': song_removal_ids, 'song_keep_count': len(song_keep_ids)})
```

An initial library album is retained if it is liked or if all of its observed song IDs belong to the downloaded-song set; all other initial album IDs are removal candidates and must be reviewed before mutation.

```python
initial_album_library_ids = {record['album_id'] for record in album_library_records}
liked_album_ids = {record['album_id'] for record in liked_album_records}
downloaded_album_ids = {record['album_id'] for record in album_library_records if set(record['song_ids']).issubset(downloaded_song_ids)}
album_keep_ids = initial_album_library_ids & (liked_album_ids | downloaded_album_ids)
album_removal_ids = sorted(initial_album_library_ids - album_keep_ids)
print({'album_removal_count': len(album_removal_ids), 'album_removal_ids': album_removal_ids, 'album_keep_count': len(album_keep_ids)})
```

